show/133515418.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T16:40:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133515528,imgsize-703626.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman bought family farm in 1908, spent decades painting and birdwatching, then left it as sanctuary]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133535152.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Mabel Norman Cerio turned her 1908 purchase of Paradise Farm in Middletown, Rhode Island, into a lifelong connection with art, wildlife and conservation. An artist and birdwatcher, she planned a bird sanctuary during her lifetime and later left the property to the community through her trust. After her death in 1949, the land became the Norman Bird Sanctuary, which today protects 300 acres of coastal habitat, six miles of trails and diverse wildlife. Her legacy also includes her paintings, sculpture interests and historic links to artists in Europe.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-rhode-island-woman-bought-her-familys-coastal-farm-in-1908-spent-decades-painting-and-birdwatching-there-then-left-the-land-to-become-a-sanctuary-that-now-protects-300-acres/articleshow/133535152.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-rhode-island-woman-bought-her-familys-coastal-farm-in-1908-spent-decades-painting-and-birdwatching-there-then-left-the-land-to-become-a-sanctuary-that-now-protects-300-acres/articleshow/133535152.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133536041,imgsize-71261.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Thousands of ancient brains survived for 12,000 years; scientists uncover why]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133534694.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Recent studies shed light on how some ancient brains manage to endure over time. The availability of oxygen is pivotal in influencing the survival of brain proteins post-mortem. In moist, low-oxygen environments, decomposition favors protein cross-linking, which fortifies these proteins against degradation. This explains the remarkable preservation of certain ancient brains while other bodily tissues succumb to decay.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-human-brain-usually-decays-first-after-death-so-how-have-thousands-survived-for-12000-years-scientists-uncover-the-chemistry-behind-the-mystery/articleshow/133534694.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-human-brain-usually-decays-first-after-death-so-how-have-thousands-survived-for-12000-years-scientists-uncover-the-chemistry-behind-the-mystery/articleshow/133534694.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T13:59:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133534940,imgsize-1252433.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Les Paul’s New Jersey home sold for $990K, then demolished; son says family got no warning]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133536815.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The New Jersey home of guitarist Les Paul was demolished shortly after its sale.  This property served as his workshop and laboratory for recording innovations.  His son expressed deep pain and questioned the lack of family notification.  Efforts were made to save historically significant materials from the damaged house.  The demolition raises broader questions about preserving creative history and private property.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/les-pauls-7-acre-new-jersey-home-studio-and-workshop-sold-for-990000-in-july-weeks-later-the-property-where-he-pioneered-multitrack-recording-was-demolished-and-his-son-says-the-family-got-no-warning/articleshow/133536815.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/les-pauls-7-acre-new-jersey-home-studio-and-workshop-sold-for-990000-in-july-weeks-later-the-property-where-he-pioneered-multitrack-recording-was-demolished-and-his-son-says-the-family-got-no-warning/articleshow/133536815.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T15:40:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133537370,imgsize-903398.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MIT class project becomes $850M plan for 8-motor hybrid aircraft factory]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133536701.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2017-an-mit-class-project-explored-a-new-kind-of-aircraft-it-has-now-grown-into-an-850-million-ohio-factory-plan-for-an-8-motor-hybrid-plane-that-can-take-off-from-an-area-about-the-length-of-a-soccer-field/articleshow/133536701.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2017-an-mit-class-project-explored-a-new-kind-of-aircraft-it-has-now-grown-into-an-850-million-ohio-factory-plan-for-an-8-motor-hybrid-plane-that-can-take-off-from-an-area-about-the-length-of-a-soccer-field/articleshow/133536701.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T15:43:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133536759,imgsize-109398.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cloud seeding drones produce 19 million gallons of water in Alaska in 3 hours]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133536074.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A pioneering climate-tech startup claims its drones have successfully induced millions of gallons of extra rainfall in Alaska. By targeting existing clouds and promoting ice crystal growth, this technology could provide vital support for drought-affected regions in the American West. The Alaska trials sought to measure the precipitation output, a crucial step forward. Future assessments will be essential in confirming the method's reliability and broader application.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cloud-seeding-drones-generate-19-million-gallons-of-water-in-alaska-in-just-three-hours-raising-hopes-for-drought-hit-regions/articleshow/133536074.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cloud-seeding-drones-generate-19-million-gallons-of-water-in-alaska-in-just-three-hours-raising-hopes-for-drought-hit-regions/articleshow/133536074.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T16:05:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133536310,imgsize-222376.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin former Optum director sentenced to 3 years in prison over $950,000 fraud scheme]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133538404.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-former-optum-director-sentenced-to-3-years-in-prison-over-950000-fraud-scheme/articleshow/133538404.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-former-optum-director-sentenced-to-3-years-in-prison-over-950000-fraud-scheme/articleshow/133538404.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T16:30:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133538722,imgsize-857831.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Albert Einstein: "If a cluttered desk is a sign of a…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133535869.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Albert Einstein questioned the assumption that a cluttered desk signifies a disorganised mind.  He suggested that an empty desk does not automatically indicate clarity or productivity.  People possess diverse thinking and working styles which influence their environments.  Creative processes can appear chaotic, reflecting experimentation rather than a lack of discipline.  Ultimately, a person's ability to think and create matters more than their workspace appearance.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/quote-of-the-day-by-albert-einstein-if-a-cluttered-desk-is-a-sign-of-a-cluttered-mind-of-what-then/articleshow/133535869.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/quote-of-the-day-by-albert-einstein-if-a-cluttered-desk-is-a-sign-of-a-cluttered-mind-of-what-then/articleshow/133535869.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T15:04:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133535899,imgsize-724980.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin Toronto man found dead at home; homicide angle being probed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133536766.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-toronto-man-found-dead-at-home-homicide-angle-being-probed/articleshow/133536766.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-toronto-man-found-dead-at-home-homicide-angle-being-probed/articleshow/133536766.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T15:32:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133537198,imgsize-546915.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Next Atlantic storm to be named 'Dolly' in an uncanny 'coincidence']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133532631.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/next-atlantic-storm-to-be-named-dolly-in-an-uncanny-coincidence/articleshow/133532631.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/next-atlantic-storm-to-be-named-dolly-in-an-uncanny-coincidence/articleshow/133532631.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T14:45:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133535926,imgsize-476265.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Scottish scholar and his American wife bought an island, spent decades preserving Gaelic culture]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133533553.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Scottish Gaelic scholar John Lorne Campbell and American musician Margaret Fay Shaw bought the remote islands of Canna and Sanday in 1938 and made Canna House their home. For decades, they collected Gaelic songs, stories, photographs and historical records. In 1981, Campbell gifted Canna, their home and their extensive collections to the National Trust for Scotland, preserving their life’s work for future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-scottish-scholar-and-his-american-wife-bought-the-remote-island-of-canna-43-years-later-they-gifted-it-their-home-and-their-lifes-work-preserving-gaelic-culture-to-the-national-trust-for-scotland/articleshow/133533553.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-scottish-scholar-and-his-american-wife-bought-the-remote-island-of-canna-43-years-later-they-gifted-it-their-home-and-their-lifes-work-preserving-gaelic-culture-to-the-national-trust-for-scotland/articleshow/133533553.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T14:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133533925,imgsize-101426.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ancient DNA reveals two unknown human lineages hidden in modern genomes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133531501.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-found-traces-of-two-unknown-ancient-human-lineages-hiding-in-modern-dna-one-split-from-our-ancestors-about-800000-years-ago-another-around-1-8-million-years-ago/articleshow/133531501.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-found-traces-of-two-unknown-ancient-human-lineages-hiding-in-modern-dna-one-split-from-our-ancestors-about-800000-years-ago-another-around-1-8-million-years-ago/articleshow/133531501.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T13:15:00+05:30</pubDa