em/articleshow/133534809.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T14:12:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133535002,imgsize-1118278.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How a family reunion in China ended in a 3-year prison term for artist Gao Zhen]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133533651.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chinese artist Gao Zhen received a three-year prison sentence for his satirical artwork.  Authorities charged him with "infringing upon the reputation of heroes" for his art.  Gao's wife expressed deep disappointment and sadness over the unexpected conviction.  His supporters argue the artworks predate the law under which he was prosecuted.  The sentence highlights China's narrowing space for artistic and political expression.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/how-a-family-reunion-in-china-ended-in-a-3-year-prison-term-for-artist-gao-zhen/articleshow/133533651.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/how-a-family-reunion-in-china-ended-in-a-3-year-prison-term-for-artist-gao-zhen/articleshow/133533651.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T13:11:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133533893,imgsize-224906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Columbia engineers develop pigment-free coating that kept surfaces 6°C cooler under Arizona sun]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133532403.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Columbia Engineering researchers developed a porous polymer coating that can cool surfaces belo